{
 "_comment": [
  "Default bindings for the controllers this package declares, by the names the controls",
  "have (P1 A, P1 Main Stick X): the frontend matches a binding to a control by its exact",
  "name (chimera#284 - written without the port, none applied). check-keybinds.py holds it.",
  "The frontend ships no bindings of its own, and the user's own bindings always win.",
  "",
  "Port 1 takes the keyboard, the first joystick (J1) and the first XInput pad (X1); ports",
  "2 to 4 take the second to fourth pads only. The face buttons follow the pad's own",
  "geometry: A is the big center button and takes the key under the hand, B sits below-left",
  "of it, X to the right, Y on top. Z is the purple shoulder tab above R. A pad's sticks",
  "drive the sticks in full (any angle, any distance); the keyboard arrows drive the MAIN",
  "STICK at full tilt, because that is how a GameCube game is steered; the d-pad, a",
  "secondary control on this pad, takes IJKL. Triggers are the analog travel; L and R the",
  "clicks at the bottom of it."
 ],
